  "notes": [
    "Inspected all actual final-package paired scenes, gates, 15 preview/commerce/meter screens and both full mobile Chromium result panels. No visible lighting/art regression found. Approved Gruvepappa v28 is preserved.",
    "Fixed-light rendering is not lossless: most static cases have maximum channel differences of 3–6/255; actual gates at most 2/255. Larger hub deltas (up to 38/255) localize to the animated elevator disc. The original/control frames also vary there. All comparison statistics are retained, without filtering out the larger deltas.",
    "Preview test now waits for deferred fixed-field baking and the following GPU draw before its first reference; neither exact restoration assertion nor repaint assertion was relaxed. Final raw current/restored images are identical.",
    "All ten current gameplay cases, invariant checks and both exported flavor checks passed. All eleven final-package jobs passed; no web GL warnings.",
    "180.303 s hub and 180.669 s Mossvein browser probes include 70.011 s and 70.046 s restored windows, original light/shadow counts, unchanged DPR/framebuffer, cancellation, focus and real mobile tap restoration.",
    "Paired final Mesa FPS: hub 3.875 -> 5.809 -> 3.983; mossvein 4.572 -> 5.044 -> 4.668 (original -> cache -> restored). These are relative software-renderer measurements, not physical iPhone predictions.",
    "Lifecycle test observed hub GPU memory 482.813 -> 502.523 MiB and Mossvein 544.993 -> 547.190 MiB after visiting the hub. Reconfiguration returned to the same allocation; temporary bake viewports were freed. Per-frame sampling is an observed peak, not a guarantee of the instantaneous maximum.",
    "Probe-lock deferral, activation, original flag/mask restoration, unsupported shadow-light fallback and repeated configure recovery pass on the exact final package.",
    "Published DEV8 still drops to 34.7 FPS in the supplied 52-second follow-up. Physical DEV9 result is pending. Do not claim the delayed iPhone FPS issue is fixed."
  ],
